    "import jax; print(\"jax backend:\", jax.default_backend())\n",
    "from moscot.problems.time import TemporalProblem\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "tp = TemporalProblem(a)\n",
    "tp = tp.score_genes_for_marginals(gene_set_proliferation=CFG[\"moscot_gene_set\"], gene_set_apoptosis=CFG[\"moscot_gene_set\"])\n",
    "tp = tp.prepare(time_key=\"day\", joint_attr=CFG[\"latent\"])\n",
    "tp = tp.solve(epsilon=CFG[\"moscot_epsilon\"], tau_a=CFG[\"moscot_tau_a\"], tau_b=CFG[\"moscot_tau_b\"], scale_cost=\"mean\")\n",
    "print(f\"solved {len(tp.problems)} coupling(s) in {time.time()-t0:.0f}s\")\n",
    "for k, pr in tp.problems.items(): print(f\"  {k}: converged={pr.solution.converged}  cost={pr.solution.cost:.4g}\")\n",
    "verify(\"every moscot coupling converged\", all(pr.solution.converged for pr in tp.problems.values()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b93f7b85",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 — RealTimeKernel, with the dead-row repair\n",
    "\n",
    "Verbatim from your cell 30: the stitched couplings can leave all-zero rows (cells no coupling reached), which the CellRank setter rejects at rtol 1e-12. Repair = within-day uniform row, exact renormalisation. Mouse hit this with 6 rows; human did not."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "9ad41a86",
   "metadata": {},
